WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.512 --> 00:00:01.867
(audience cheering and clapping)

00:00:01.867 --> 00:00:03.450
- [Kelly] You look so nice.

00:00:03.450 --> 00:00:06.600
- Thank you, I wore a suit
and everything for you, Kelly.

00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:08.423
- I've never seen a dentist
that looks like you, my man.

00:00:08.423 --> 00:00:10.560
- Ah!
- I was like, "What?"

00:00:10.560 --> 00:00:11.497
- That's true, I was gonna be a dentist.

00:00:11.497 --> 00:00:12.710
- [Kelly] You really were?

00:00:12.710 --> 00:00:13.543
- I mean, that's what
I went to school for.

00:00:13.543 --> 00:00:15.510
I was gonna, I got my degree in biology.

00:00:15.510 --> 00:00:16.343
- [Kelly] Oh, that's so cool.

00:00:16.343 --> 00:00:17.910
- With the intention to
go into dental school.

00:00:17.910 --> 00:00:18.743
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:19.864 --> 00:00:21.690
- And I think the reason
I wanted to do it was

00:00:21.690 --> 00:00:24.607
because my mom pushed me
at an early age and say,

00:00:24.607 --> 00:00:25.560
"What are you gonna do with your life?"

00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:26.730
I was like, I'm an eighth grader.

00:00:26.730 --> 00:00:27.563
I don't know.

00:00:27.563 --> 00:00:28.396
- Yeah, what?

00:00:28.396 --> 00:00:29.670
- So my sophomore year I told her

00:00:29.670 --> 00:00:31.440
that I wanted to be a dentist because A

00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:33.360
I could check off the
box of being a doctor,

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:34.672
which would please my mother.

00:00:34.672 --> 00:00:35.650
- (laughs) Get it in there.

00:00:35.650 --> 00:00:37.797
- And B I was always good at drawing and

00:00:37.797 --> 00:00:39.360
and making things with my hands.

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:40.590
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:40.590 --> 00:00:41.550
- So I think that was the reason.

00:00:41.550 --> 00:00:42.383
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:42.383 --> 00:00:43.770
And then, and then I got completely jaded

00:00:43.770 --> 00:00:45.420
and moved to Los Angeles, and here we are.

00:00:45.420 --> 00:00:46.800
- I know. It worked out.
(audience applauds)

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:48.450
It worked out for the better.
(Josh laughs)

00:00:48.450 --> 00:00:49.283
I think. I think.

00:00:49.283 --> 00:00:52.050
But you literally are just back
from your honeymoon, right?

00:00:52.050 --> 00:00:52.970
- Yes.

00:00:52.970 --> 00:00:54.406
- [Kelly] Congratulations
on getting married.

00:00:54.406 --> 00:00:55.698
(audience cheering)
- Mm-hmm. Thank you.

00:00:55.698 --> 00:00:56.531
- [Kelly] That's awesome.

00:00:56.531 --> 00:00:58.200
How was the honeymoon?

00:00:58.200 --> 00:00:59.160
Oh my God, so great.

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:01.260
- [Josh] Look at that
beautiful Ralph Lauren suit.

00:01:01.260 --> 00:01:02.486
Thank you.

00:01:02.486 --> 00:01:03.960
- Yeah. Look at that dress.

00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:05.490
I'm sorry, I wasn't looking at you.

00:01:05.490 --> 00:01:07.987
Yeah, I'm like, "She looks beautiful."

00:01:07.987 --> 00:01:10.410
- She is a little sweetheart.

00:01:10.410 --> 00:01:13.686
And we had an amazing time in Thailand.

00:01:13.686 --> 00:01:14.519
- [Kelly] Had you ever been?
- Have you been?

00:01:14.519 --> 00:01:16.170
- I have been to Thailand, a few times.

00:01:16.170 --> 00:01:19.080
- Well, it takes you about a
full 24 hours to get there.

00:01:19.080 --> 00:01:20.610
- [Kelly] Yeah.
- So it took us a day or two

00:01:20.610 --> 00:01:22.080
just to get acclimated to the time.

00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:25.680
But we went to this beautiful
resort called Soneva

00:01:25.680 --> 00:01:27.090
on this little island in Thailand

00:01:27.090 --> 00:01:28.140
for about four or five days.

00:01:28.140 --> 00:01:31.484
And then we went to Bangkok,
which is a complete-

00:01:31.484 --> 00:01:32.670
- Totally different.

00:01:32.670 --> 00:01:35.460
- Departure from the serenity of Soneva.

00:01:35.460 --> 00:01:36.470
- Yeah, is it true that you had to go

00:01:36.470 --> 00:01:37.590
to the emergency room, like

00:01:37.590 --> 00:01:39.030
right before the wedding?
- [Josh] I did.

00:01:39.030 --> 00:01:39.930
- That's a good start.

00:01:39.930 --> 00:01:41.220
- Well, yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:01:41.220 --> 00:01:42.053
Tell me about it.

00:01:42.053 --> 00:01:43.440
So it was like,

00:01:43.440 --> 00:01:45.990
we had this amazing band
play for the rehearsal dinner

00:01:45.990 --> 00:01:46.823
the night before.

00:01:46.823 --> 00:01:47.656
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:50.760
And we had a blast.

00:01:50.760 --> 00:01:52.980
And afterwards we went into the party bus

00:01:52.980 --> 00:01:54.630
to go back to the hotel and we had music

00:01:54.630 --> 00:01:55.860
pumping in there.
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:55.860 --> 00:01:56.693
- I'm feeling good.
- [Kelly] Feeling good.

00:01:56.693 --> 00:01:58.290
- So I decide I'm gonna start dancing.

00:01:58.290 --> 00:02:00.300
And they have those handles

00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:01.471
that you hold on in the party bus.

00:02:01.471 --> 00:02:02.304
- So let loose.

00:02:02.304 --> 00:02:03.780
- I tried to do this thing
where you like a gymnast,

00:02:03.780 --> 00:02:05.010
like straighten myself out.

00:02:05.010 --> 00:02:06.030
And I was like, "egh oh."

00:02:06.030 --> 00:02:06.877
- Cause we have really good
ideas when we're inebriated.

00:02:06.877 --> 00:02:08.677
- Something just happened.

00:02:08.677 --> 00:02:09.510
(Kelly gasps)
(audience laughs)

00:02:09.510 --> 00:02:11.340
And yeah, so I felt fine.

00:02:11.340 --> 00:02:13.500
I got through that night and
I wake up the next morning,

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:17.820
two hours before the wedding
and I couldn't get out of bed.

00:02:17.820 --> 00:02:19.080
I literally couldn't stand up.

00:02:19.080 --> 00:02:20.850
So I was like, "What
am I gonna do? Oh my."

00:02:20.850 --> 00:02:22.216
So they had to take me
to the emergency room,

00:02:22.216 --> 00:02:26.246
give a bunch of meds, and
shoot me with Toradol.

00:02:26.246 --> 00:02:27.480
- Oh my Gosh.
- And it was great.

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:29.070
Everything went great.
(audience laughing)

00:02:29.070 --> 00:02:29.903
I got through the night.

00:02:29.903 --> 00:02:31.320
- Of course it was, you're
on Toradol (laughs).

00:02:31.320 --> 00:02:35.400
- Danced the night away, next
morning after the wedding.

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:36.780
Couldn't get out of bed again.

00:02:36.780 --> 00:02:37.613
- [Kelly] Oh no.

00:02:37.613 --> 00:02:38.700
- They had to take me
to the emergency room

00:02:38.700 --> 00:02:39.660
again the next night.

00:02:39.660 --> 00:02:41.640
And she's like, "Oh my God,
everything's fine here.

00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:43.170
This is like the first day of my marriage,

00:02:43.170 --> 00:02:45.600
and I'm wheeling my husband
around in a wheelchair."

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:47.072
I'm already way older than she is.

00:02:47.072 --> 00:02:47.905
(laughing)

00:02:47.905 --> 00:02:50.190
So it wasn't a great start.

00:02:50.190 --> 00:02:51.180
- [Kelly] A funny one.

00:02:51.180 --> 00:02:52.110
- But.
- [Kelly] Memorable.

00:02:52.110 --> 00:02:53.820
- I was like, Babe, for better or worse.

00:02:53.820 --> 00:02:55.360
- Yeah. You said so, I heard it.

00:02:55.360 --> 00:02:57.300
(audience laughing and applauding)

00:02:57.300 --> 00:02:58.454
That's incredible.

00:02:58.454 --> 00:03:01.110
So your honeymoon was in Thailand,

00:03:01.110 --> 00:03:04.170
but you also just posted this.

00:03:04.170 --> 00:03:05.195
Oh, I love this.

00:03:05.195 --> 00:03:06.395
- [Josh] Oh yeah.

00:03:06.395 --> 00:03:08.160
This is my cabin out in Minnesota.

00:03:08.160 --> 00:03:09.990
- [Kelly] Who's getting
hypothermia in the-

00:03:09.990 --> 00:03:13.077
- So that's my cousin Dallas.

00:03:13.077 --> 00:03:15.270
What we do is we take a chainsaw,

00:03:15.270 --> 00:03:16.697
and cut a big hole in the ice.

00:03:16.697 --> 00:03:18.510
- [Kelly] Yeah, to go ice fishing.

00:03:18.510 --> 00:03:19.369
- Well, no, no, no.

00:03:19.369 --> 00:03:20.880
You do ice plunge,

00:03:20.880 --> 00:03:22.884
you get into the water and you, like-

00:03:22.884 --> 00:03:23.880
- And some of us ice fish.

00:03:23.880 --> 00:03:25.140
- Yes. Some people ice fish.

00:03:25.140 --> 00:03:26.610
We get into the water and we ice fish.

00:03:26.610 --> 00:03:29.130
But we have this old wood burning stove

00:03:29.130 --> 00:03:31.200
that we found on the property years ago

00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:34.050
