some kind of a fishing shed.

00:03:34.050 --> 00:03:35.490
And we realize, no, this is a,

00:03:35.490 --> 00:03:37.530
like, an old wood burning sauna.

00:03:37.530 --> 00:03:40.380
So you put wood in the
side of it, it heats up.

00:03:40.380 --> 00:03:41.400
And that's like the, you know,

00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:43.015
the Scandinavians used to do it.

00:03:43.015 --> 00:03:43.848
- [Kelly] That's cool.

00:03:43.848 --> 00:03:44.681
- So we'll go into the ice,

00:03:44.681 --> 00:03:46.140
then we'll get in the the
sauna and go back and forth.

00:03:46.140 --> 00:03:46.973
- That's so cool.

00:03:46.973 --> 00:03:47.806
Do you find that important?

00:03:47.806 --> 00:03:48.639
I have a ranch.

00:03:48.639 --> 00:03:50.430
I go escape and I like
getting out of the city.

00:03:50.430 --> 00:03:51.690
- Yep.
- Is that important to you?

00:03:51.690 --> 00:03:52.523
- Oh my gosh.

00:03:52.523 --> 00:03:54.075
It's everything for me, I mean, it's,

00:03:54.075 --> 00:03:56.970
for me to get, I always say
every time I get out there

00:03:56.970 --> 00:03:59.002
it's like my blood pressure drops about

00:03:59.002 --> 00:04:00.652
twenty-five percent
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:04:00.652 --> 00:04:02.473
And then you question life decisions

00:04:02.473 --> 00:04:03.591
